sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: route:destroy
  %% kind: route.destroy
  %% Proposed ADR 0271 path. Names below describe resource effects; primitive names are settled with the implementation.
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=executor tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>Orbit caller
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>admission
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Route Node<br/>executor
  participant V as VPN Node<br/>DNS executor
  CLI->>GW: route:destroy ROUTE
  Note over GW: Check access and target
  %%> Keep the existing admission guards and publication holds. The eligible first plan is an ordinary private Route, without replacement or offline residue.
  alt covered private Route and every target advertises support
    GW->>EN: Admit engine Operation
    GW-->>CLI: Operation accepted
    %%> The kind must be enabled. Admission selects one owner for the full Operation.
    opt plan withdraws DNS
      EN->>V: Withdraw owned DNS answers
      %%> Update records and catalog under the existing revision and ownership checks. Keep other Routes' records intact.
      V-->>EN: DNS change verified
      opt DNS grace applies
        Note over EN: Wait for DNS expiry<br/>31 seconds
        %%> Use a durable deadline. A redelivered receipt must not skip the grace. This chart covers the standalone Route command.
      end
    end
    EN->>N: Withdraw site and leaf
    %%> Use the admitted site, leaf and ownership revision. Validate before reload and refuse a foreign change.
    opt development pools affected
      EN->>N: Converge PHP pools
    end
    EN->>N: Verify owned state absent
    %%> Exercise a sibling Route on the same Node. Keep --offline, replacements, ingress and Router/LAN cleanup on the established path for this first scope.
    N-->>EN: Withdrawal verified
    alt verified receipt
      EN->>GW: Remove Route record
    else signed step failed
      EN->>GW: Record the failed step
    else receipt missing
      Note over EN: Recover the signed step
      %%> A missing receipt allows redelivery for the same Operation step. Recover its journaled result or verify the owned state before settlement. A deterministic refusal records the failed step; retain the domain's existing failure state.
    end
  else unsupported Node plan
    Note over GW: Use existing Route removal
    %%> Decide before dispatch. An accepted engine Operation keeps its owner through recovery.
  end
